<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"></head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:24px 12px;background:#f3f5f7;color:#24313d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;line-height:1.6;">
<table role="presentation" style="width:100%;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;background:#fff;border:1px solid #dce2e7;border-radius:8px;">
<tr><td style="padding:24px;">
<p>Hi <%= ERB::Util.html_escape(@user.login) %>,</p>
<p>This is a reminder about the IP addresses below, which are still unassigned and planned for release.</p>
<% if @addresses.any?(&:public_ipv4?) -%>
<p>Public IPv4 addresses are a scarce resource. Releasing addresses you no longer need helps make room for other VPSes.</p>
<% end -%>
<ul>
<% @addresses.each do |item| -%>
  <li><%= ERB::Util.html_escape(item.address) %>/<%= item.prefix %> (<%= ERB::Util.html_escape(item.location_label || 'location unavailable') %>)</li>
<% end -%>
</ul>
<p><strong>Planned release date:</strong> <%= ERB::Util.html_escape(local_time(@campaign.deadline, '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M %Z')) %></p>
<p>If you no longer need these addresses, you do not need to reply or do anything.</p>
<p>If you still need an address, you can keep it by assigning it to a VPS.
<% if @campaign.allow_keep -%>
You can also keep an address unassigned: select it in vpsAdmin and enter a reason why you need it.
<% else -%>
Keeping an unassigned address requires an administrator's exemption. Previously submitted reasons do not prevent release under the current policy.
<% end -%>
</p>
<p>You can see the current address status and options for keeping them in vpsAdmin:</p>
<p style="margin:24px 0;"><a href="<%= ERB::Util.html_escape(@webui_url) %>/?page=ip_release&amp;action=request&amp;id=<%= @request.id %>" style="display:inline-block;padding:12px 20px;background:#176b99;border-radius:5px;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:bold;">Open in vpsAdmin</a></p>
<p>Thank you for helping make unused addresses available to other users.</p>
<p>Best regards,<br>vpsAdmin</p>
</td></tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
